Surface summary (parity port of the web query-aware redirect):
  The web component is routing-only: it reads useLocation(), maps the legacy ?tab= value to the new
  Notifications route (TAB_TO_ROUTE: alerts->/notifications/alerts, history->/notifications/inbox,
  preferences->/notifications/quiet-hours; default + unknown -> /notifications/alerts), forwards every
  OTHER query param (filter, q, page, severity, vehicle_id, rule_id, ...) and returns <Navigate to replace />.
  The native surface reproduces this verbatim in a WinUI-free resolver (LegacyAlertsRedirectResolver) with a
  faithful application/x-www-form-urlencoded parse/serialize round-trip (URLSearchParams parity), binds the
  current location through the P1/S8 state-holder seam (ILegacyAlertsLocationSource, the useLocation analogue),
  resolves the destination in the LegacyAlertsRedirectViewModel, and -- because a WinUI control must render
  something where React returns <Navigate> -- shows an accessible "Redirecting..." affordance (ProgressRing +
  i18n status notifications.legacyRedirect.status + polite live region) before raising NavigationRequested so
  the host performs the replacing navigation. view.opened telemetry emits slug=LegacyAlertsRedirect (P1/S11),
  PII-safe (never logs the location/query).

States (web parity): the web source performs a SYNCHRONOUS client-side redirect with NO network read, so it
  has exactly one branch and deliberately no loading/empty/error/stale/offline state. The native surface
  documents this absence (LegacyAlertsRedirectState.Redirecting) exactly as the sibling presentational
  redirect-free surfaces do, and still renders a non-blank, accessible redirecting affordance.

--- PRE-EXISTING baseline blockers fixed to reach a green gate (integration-merge accidents, documented; no silent drift) ---
  B1. apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj was committed at HEAD with TWO <Project>
      roots plus tangled comment prose containing literal tags (MSB4025: "The 'Compile' start tag on line 168
      does not match the end tag of 'Project'"), so the whole solution failed XML load and NOTHING built. This
      is the exact "chain of integration merges re-concatenated multiple roots" failure the file's own
      INVARIANT comment warns about. Consolidated back to ONE canonical root with a single path-sorted,
      deduplicated Compile item group = the union of all 519 previously-linked sources (no link dropped;
      verified by diffing HEAD vs new include sets) PLUS the 3 new LegacyAlertsRedirect Model/Source/ViewModel
      links. This is the same consolidation every prior feature-view prompt performed (see 0178/0163/0158/...).
  B2. enum DrivetrainHealth { Good, Warning, Critical } had been deleted from BOTH HealthOverview.Model.cs and
      HealthRecommendations.Model.cs by a bad merge dedup -- each file's comment claimed the OTHER file held the
      canonical definition, so neither did (41x CS0246/CS0103 "DrivetrainHealth could not be found" across
      HealthOverview/HealthRecommendations + their tests). This single missing C# type also CASCADED into the
      WinUI markup compiler (WMC9999 NRE + ~95 spurious "Unknown type Ts*" WMC0001/WMC0110) because the XAML
      compiler could not build the project reference assembly. Restored the single canonical definition once in
      HealthOverview.Model.cs (where HealthRecommendations.Model.cs's surviving comment already pointed), which
      resolved all 41 C# errors AND the entire XAML cascade. Unrelated to LegacyAlertsRedirect but strictly
      required: without it the test project cannot compile and the solution cannot build.

